{"name":"Leisure Time","hex":"#758c8f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"leisure time","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Free time."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leisure_time"}],"entries":[{"title":"Leisure Time","blocks":[{"text":"Awqat Faragh IPA: [ʔæwˈʔæːt fɑˈɾɑːɣ] is a 2006 Egyptian film about a group of Middle Class youths and their experiences growing up and dealing with drugs and sex. The film was the first appearance for actors Ahmed Hatem, Karim Kassem and Amr Abed."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d4/AwqatFaraghMoviePoster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leisure_Time","wikidata":"Q11161083"},{"title":"Leisure","blocks":[{"text":"Leisure has often been defined as a quality of experience or as free time. Free time is time spent away from business, work, job hunting, domestic chores, and education, as well as necessary activities such as eating and sleeping. Leisure as an experience usually emphasizes dimensions of perceived freedom and choice. It is done for \"its own sake\", for the quality of experience and involvement. Other classic definitions include Thorstein Veblen's (1899) of \"nonproductive consumption of time.\" Free time is not easy to define due to the multiplicity of approaches used to determine its essence. Different disciplines have definitions reflecting their common issues: for example, sociology on social forces and contexts and psychology as mental and emotional states and conditions. From a research perspective, these approaches have an advantage of being quantifiable and comparable over time and place."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Tompkins_Square_Park_Central_Knoll.jpg/330px-Tompkins_Square_Park_Central_Knoll.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leisure","wikidata":"Q180910"},{"title":"Time","blocks":[{"text":"Time is the continuous progression of existence that occurs in an apparently irreversible succession from the past, through the present, and into the future. Time dictates all forms of action, age, and causality, being a component quantity of various measurements used to sequence events, to compare the duration of events or the intervals between them, and to quantify rates of change of quantities in material reality or in conscious experience. Time is often referred to as the fourth dimension and the temporal dimension, in addition to the three spatial dimensions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/MontreGousset001.jpg/330px-MontreGousset001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time","wikidata":"Q11471"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Man-relaxing.jpg/500px-Man-relaxing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Man-relaxing.jpg/1280px-Man-relaxing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Man-relaxing.jpg/500px-Man-relaxing.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A man relaxing on a couch","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMan-relaxing.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Oasis_de_Pica._I_regi%C3%B3n..jpg/500px-Oasis_de_Pica._I_regi%C3%B3n..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Oasis_de_Pica._I_regi%C3%B3n..jpg/1280px-Oasis_de_Pica._I_regi%C3%B3n..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Oasis_de_Pica._I_regi%C3%B3n..jpg/500px-Oasis_de_Pica._I_regi%C3%B3n..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Leisure time swimming at an oasis","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOasis_de_Pica._I_regi%C3%B3n..jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/DV257_no.10_The_start.png/500px-DV257_no.10_The_start.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/DV257_no.10_The_start.png/500px-DV257_no.10_The_start.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A caricature of upper class Victorian tourists, 1852","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADV257_no.10_The_start.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/VietnamCombatArtCAT04JamesPollockGICardgame.jpg/500px-VietnamCombatArtCAT04JamesPollockGICardgame.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/VietnamCombatArtCAT04JamesPollockGICardgame.jpg/500px-VietnamCombatArtCAT04JamesPollockGICardgame.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"GI Card Game, watercolor by James Pollock,  U. S. Army Vietnam Combat Artists Team IV (CAT IV 1967). During the Vietnam War soldiers waiting to go on patrol would sometimes spend their leisure time playing cards. Courtesy National Museum of the United States Army.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVietnamCombatArtCAT04JamesPollockGICardgame.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Wooden_hourglass_3.jpg/500px-Wooden_hourglass_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Wooden_hourglass_3.jpg/500px-Wooden_hourglass_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_co